WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.690
Two cyclists compare their speeds.

2
00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:06.230
One says, I averaged
eighteen kilometres an hour.

3
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:10.270
The other says, I averaged five
point six metres per second.

4
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.790
Eighteen sounds far bigger.

5
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.870
But the two numbers
are in different units,

6
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.230
so you can't compare them yet.

7
00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:21.170
So who was really faster, and
how do you convert safely?

8
00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:23.890
In this mission, you'll
meet the S I base units,

9
00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.650
and see how other units
are built from them.

10
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.650
You'll use prefixes such as kilo
and milli as powers of ten,

11
00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:34.150
and convert between
units step by step.

12
00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:38.330
Your mission: work out which
cyclist was really faster.
